course: dictionary
lesson: 12367
title: Cropped: cut short or turned up
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Cropped is the past form of the verb crop. Crop means to cut something short, like hair, grass or the edges of a picture. «Mia had her hair cropped before the summer.» This means her hair was cut very short.
explain: Cropped can also describe clothes. «She wore a cropped top and blue jeans.» A cropped top has been cut short on purpose, so it stops above the waist.
explain: Cropped up is a different meaning. «A problem cropped up just before the match.» Here cropped up means appeared suddenly, without anyone expecting it. Read the words around it: is the sentence about cutting, or about something appearing?
fact: Crop means to cut something short, and cropped is its past form.
fact: «Cropped» can describe hair or clothes that have been cut short on purpose.
fact: A photo is cropped when its unwanted edges are cut off.
fact: «Crop up» means to appear or happen suddenly, without being expected.
fact: A field that has been cropped has had crops grown or cut on it.
exercise: «Sam had his hair cropped for the summer.» What does cropped mean here? | *Cut very short | Curled and long | Dyed bright green | Washed and dried
exercise: «The photo was cropped to show only the dog.» What does cropped mean here? | Made bigger and clearer | Printed on shiny paper | Painted in bright colours | *Had its edges cut off
exercise: «A problem cropped up just before the match.» What does cropped up mean? | Was grown in a field | *Appeared suddenly, without warning | Was cut into small pieces | Was lost for ever
test: «She wore cropped trousers that stopped below her knees.» What does cropped mean here? | Very dirty and torn | Long and baggy | Made of thick wool | *Cut short on purpose
test: Which word is the past form of the verb crop? | Crept | Crowded | Cropping | *Cropped
exam: «The farmer's field had been cropped all summer.» What does cropped mean in this sentence? | *Had crops grown or cut on it | Fenced off for animals | Flooded with water | Covered in snow
